  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-2}{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-{x}^{-1}]}_{a}^{-2} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{x}]}_{a}^{-2} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\frac{1}{(-2)}-\\frac{1}{a}] \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
